From 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 21:45:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iommu: qcom: add MSM8660 compatible

MSM8660 uses the same first-generation Qualcomm IOMMU DT interface as
APQ8064. Allow an SoC-specific compatible followed by the existing
APQ8064 fallback.

Keep the existing binding interrupt order unchanged: non-secure first,
secure second. Sony's MSM8x60 resources use that same ordering.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/iommu/qcom,apq8064-iommu.yaml | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/qcom,apq8064-iommu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/qcom,apq8064-iommu.yaml
index dc45a2356f06..123456789abc 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/qcom,apq8064-iommu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/qcom,apq8064-iommu.yaml
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/iommu/qcom,apq8064-iommu.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Qualcomm APQ8064 IOMMU
+title: Qualcomm APQ8064 and MSM8660 IOMMU
 
 maintainers:
   - David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
@@ -16,8 +16,13 @@ description:
   outside of the CPU, each connected to the IOMMU through a port called micro-TLB.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: qcom,apq8064-iommu
+    oneOf:
+      - const: qcom,apq8064-iommu
+      - items:
+          - enum:
+              - qcom,msm8660-iommu
+          - const: qcom,apq8064-iommu
 
   clocks:
     items:
-- 
2.51.0
